TASK 7.4 — Traceability check against requirements_app.md
CAVEAT: requirements_app.md is not present in this repository (only
tasks_app.md exists under sdd/). This checklist traces against the
acceptance criteria embedded directly inside each task's description
in tasks_app.md, which states it derives from requirements_app.md/
design_app.md v1.0. If those source docs turn up, re-run this check
against their literal acceptance criteria text.
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Requirement 1 — Input & Language Selection (Tasks 2, 5.1, 5.2, 7.2)
  [x] Text input accepts typed and pasted text
      -> verified: textarea is a standard input, manual Playwright fill()
         exercises the same code path as typing/pasting.
  [x] Target-language dropdown displays the full fixed supported-language list
      -> verified: Phase 3 live check, 19 options in #target-language.
  [x] Empty text is rejected client-side with zero network calls
      -> verified: Task 7.2 scenario 2 (this report).
  [x] Missing target language is rejected client-side with zero network calls
      -> verified: Task 7.2 scenario 3 (this report).
  [x] Server-side validation is the actual source of truth (backend re-validates
      independent of client)
      -> verified: backend/tests/test_validation.py + test_api_translate.py
         Task 4.1 tests reject invalid payloads even when sent directly,
         bypassing the frontend entirely.

Requirement 2 — Detection & Translation (Tasks 2, 3, 4.1, 4.2, 4.4, 5.3, 7.1)
  [x] Given valid text + supported target language, detected source language
      and translated text are returned
      -> verified: test_translation_service.py (mocked), plus live smoke
         test and Task 7.1/7.3 live requests (real googletrans).
  [x] Library failure raises TranslationServiceError, not a raw exception
      -> verified: test_translation_service.py failure-path tests.
  [x] POST /api/translate: 200 on success with correct TranslationResponse
      -> verified: test_api_translate.py Task 4.2 test, live Task 7.1 check.
  [x] POST /api/translate: 400 INVALID_INPUT on malformed input, service
      never reached
      -> verified: test_api_translate.py Task 4.1 tests (mock_translator
         assert_not_called).
  [x] POST /api/translate: 500 TRANSLATION_FAILED on simulated service
      failure, no raw traceback exposed
      -> verified: test_api_translate.py Task 4.2 failure test.
  [x] Frontend request body matches TranslationRequest field names exactly
      -> verified: Task 7.1 (this report) — captured real fetch() body,
         keys == {text, targetLanguage} exactly.

Requirement 3 — Display & Read-Aloud (Tasks 6.1, 6.2, 7.2)
  [x] Successful response renders sourceText, detectedLanguage, translatedText
      -> verified: Phase 3 live check + Task 7.1 (this report).
  [x] Error condition renders a message, never a stale/partial result
      -> verified: Task 7.2 scenario 4 (this report) — result section
         stayed hidden when the network-failure error was shown.
  [x] Read-aloud control appears only when window.speechSynthesis exists
      -> verified: Phase 3 live check (supporting) + simulated
         non-supporting-browser check (button stays hidden).
  [x] Activating read-aloud speaks the translated text
      -> verified: Task 7.2 scenario 1 (this report) — speechSynthesis.speak()
         spied and confirmed called with the exact rendered translatedText.

Performance NFR (Tasks 2, 4.4, 7.3)
  [x] 5,000-char input limit enforced
      -> verified: test_validation.py boundary tests (5000 ok, 5001 rejected).
  [x] Sampled response times comfortably under the 3-second target
      -> verified: Task 7.3 Part B (this report) — max 1500ms across 5
         live requests, all real googletrans network calls.
  NOTE: formal load/stress testing is explicitly out of scope per
  design_app.md's stated Performance Considerations (per tasks_app.md
  Task 7.3 scope) — not silently skipped.

Security NFR (Tasks 4.3, 7.5)
  [x] Request/response text content (text, translatedText) never appears
      in log output, success or error path
      -> verified: backend/test-results/phase2_backend_test_results.log
         Task 4.3 — automated caplog tests + manual canary-string
         inspection, both passed.
  [x] Error responses never expose a raw stack trace
      -> verified: test_api_translate.py Task 4.2 failure test asserts
         no "Traceback" / raw exception text in the ErrorResponse message.
  [x] No debug code or content-logging left in source
      -> verified: Task 7.5 (this report) — repo-wide grep for
         console.log/print/debugger across app/, frontend/, tests/,
         wsgi.py returned zero matches.

Usability NFR (Tasks 6.2, 6.3)
  [x] Read-aloud degrades gracefully (hidden, not broken) without browser support
      -> verified: Phase 3 simulated non-supporting-browser check.
  [x] All controls usable at a mobile viewport (375px) without horizontal scroll
      -> verified: Phase 3 live check, body.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth.

Reliability NFR (Tasks 5.3, 6.1, 7.2)
  [x] Error response (4xx/5xx) is distinguished from network-level failure
      in how the frontend handles it
      -> verified: showError() paths differ in message text; Task 7.2
         scenario 4 (this report) shows the distinct network-failure copy
         vs. the ErrorResponse.message copy used for 400/500 (Phase 3).
  [x] No stale/partial result ever shown alongside or after an error
      -> verified: Task 7.2 scenario 4 (this report) — hideResult() is
         called unconditionally inside showError().

RESULT: every requirement/NFR line item above traces to at least one
passing automated test or a manually/programmatically verified live
behavior recorded in this report or in
backend/test-results/phase2_backend_test_results.log. No gaps found.
